\f0\b \cf2 Title:
\f1\b0  Landscaping Services in Gouldsboro, PA | Lawn Care, Mulch, Planting & Weed Control\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Meta description:
\f1\b0\fs30  ABCO Landscaping provides lawn mowing, weed control, mulch installation, planting, and basic landscape maintenance in Gouldsboro, Eagle Lake, the Poconos, and nearby Northeast PA areas.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 ABCO Landscaping provides quality, reliable landscaping services for  properties throughout Eagle Lake, Covington Township, and nearby Lackawanna communities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Our landscaping work focuses on keeping your property clean, usable, and well-maintained without overcomplications. Whether you need regular lawn mowing, fresh mulch, weed control, new plantings, or help improving curb appeal, we can help keep your outdoor space looking 
\fs28 sharp throughout the growing season.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs38 \cf2 Lawn Care & Landscape Maintenance
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 A good-looking property starts with consistent lawn and landscape care. We handle the basics that make the biggest difference: clean mowing, neat edges, controlled weeds, healthy beds, and fresh landscape materials.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Our landscaping services include:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Lawn mowing\
\'95	Weed control\
\'95	Mulch installation\
\'95	Planting\
\'95	Landscape bed refreshes\
\'95	Lawn care materials\
\'95	Stone, soil, and mulch placement\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Basic property beautification\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 We can help with one-time improvements or recurring maintenance depending on your property's needs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs38 \cf2 Lawn Mowing
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Regular mowing keeps your property looking maintained and helps prevent the lawn from becoming overgrown, uneven, or difficult to manage. We provide lawn mowing for residential properties, vacation homes, rental properties, and small commercial lots.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Our mowing service can include trimming around edges, fences, buildings, walkways, and other common areas so the property has a clean, finished look.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs38 \cf2 Weed Control
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Weeds can quickly take over lawns, driveways, walkways, mulch beds, and open landscape areas. ABCO helps control weeds before they make the property look neglected.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 We can help with weed control in:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Lawn areas\
\'95	Mulch beds\
\'95	Planting beds\
\'95	Walkway edges\
\'95	Driveway edges\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Around structures and hard-to-maintain areas\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 For many properties in the Poconos, weed control is not a one-time fix. A consistent maintenance plan usually works better than waiting until the weeds are already out of control.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs38 \cf2 Mulching
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Fresh mulch is one of the fastest ways to improve curb appeal. It gives planting beds a finished look, helps define landscape areas, and can help reduce weed growth when installed properly. Mulch also helps maintain steady soil temperature for newly planted greens.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 We install mulch around:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Walkways\
\'95	Trees and shrubs\
\'95	Flower beds\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Mulch also helps protect soil from drying out too quickly and keeps beds looking clean between maintenance visits.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs38 \cf2 Planting
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The right plants can make a property look more finished without creating constant maintenance problems. We can help with basic planting for front beds, driveway entrances, walkways, borders, and outdoor living areas.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Planting options may include:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Shrubs\
\'95	Flowers\
\'95	Evergreens\
\'95	Simple border plantings\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Low-maintenance landscape beds\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 For Pocono properties, plant choice matters. Deer, shade, rocky soil, wet areas, and cold winters can all affect what survives and what gets eaten.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs38 \cf2 Lawn Care Materials
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 We can help refresh common lawn and landscaping materials such as mulch, topsoil, decorative stone, planting soil, and bed edging materials.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Using the right material in the right area helps reduce maintenance and keeps the property cleaner. For example, mulch may work well around plantings, while decorative stone may be better in certain drainage-prone or high-traffic areas.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 Did You Know? \
Deer-Resistant Landscaping in the Poconos
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Deer are a major issue for many properties in Gouldsboro, Eagle Lake, and the Pocono region. A plant that looks great at the nursery may disappear fast if it is one of the deer's preferred foods.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 No plant is truly deer proof. Deer resistance depends on local deer pressure, weather, season, and food availability. Plants commonly described as deer-resistant are usually better choices for deer-heavy landscapes, but fencing or repellents may still be needed in high-pressure areas.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa150\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34 \cf2 Deer-resistant plants to consider
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sl276\slmult1\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	
\f0\b Daffodils / Narcissus
\f1\b0  - often a good spring bulb choice because deer usually avoid them.\
\'95	
\f0\b Barberry
\f1\b0  - very deer-resistant, but Japanese barberry is invasive and problematic in Pennsylvania, so it should generally be avoided or replaced with better alternatives.\
\'95	
\f0\b Boxwood
\f1\b0  - commonly used for structured foundation plantings.\
\'95	
\f0\b Bayberry
\f1\b0  - a strong shrub option for deer-heavy areas.\
\'95	
\f0\b American holly
\f1\b0  - can work as a more substantial evergreen/tree-form option.\
\'95	
\f0\b Juniper
\f1\b0  - often used as an evergreen shrub or groundcover.\
\'95	
\f0\b Bleeding heart
\f1\b0  - a shade-friendly perennial that can work well in woodland-style beds.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa150\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34 \cf2 \
Important note about new plantings
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Even deer-resistant plants may need protection when newly installed. Deer may test new plantings, and plants that hold up once mature may still be vulnerable early on. Newly planted shrubs, flowers, and evergreens may need temporary protection, especially during winter or early spring when deer are hungry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 More Landscaping Did You Know Ideas
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa150\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Did you know mulch can be too deep?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Mulch helps beds look clean, but piling it too high around plants or tree trunks can trap moisture and cause problems. A clean, even layer usually looks better and performs better than a heavy mound.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa150\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Did you know weed fabric is not always the best answer?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Weed fabric can help in some stone areas, but in mulch beds it can become messy over time as weeds grow on top of the fabric. For many beds, proper edging, mulch depth, and regular maintenance are more practical.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa150\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Did you know low-maintenance does not mean no-maintenance?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Even simple landscapes need trimming, weed control, mulch refreshes, and cleanup. The goal is to choose materials and plants that reduce maintenance, not eliminate it completely.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa150\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Did you know Pocono properties often need tougher plant choices?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Cold winters, deer, rocky soil, shade, and wet areas can make landscaping more difficult. Choosing the right plant for the right spot matters more than choosing plants only because they look good in photos.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa150\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Did you know evergreens can create year-round curb appeal?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Flowers are seasonal, but evergreens can keep a property looking finished even in winter. Shrubs like boxwood, holly, juniper, spruce, and pine can help create structure when annuals and perennials are dormant.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 Suggested FAQ Section
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 What landscaping services do you offer?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 We offer lawn mowing, weed control, planting, mulching, lawn care materials, and basic landscape maintenance for homes, rentals, cabins, lake properties, and small commercial properties.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Do you offer regular lawn mowing?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Yes. We provide lawn mowing for local properties in Gouldsboro, Eagle Lake, and nearby Pocono communities. Mowing can be scheduled as needed depending on the property and season.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Can you install mulch?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Yes. We install mulch in flower beds, foundation beds, around shrubs, along walkways, and in other landscape areas. Fresh mulch is one of the quickest ways to improve curb appeal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Can you help choose deer-resistant plants?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Yes. We can help choose practical planting options for deer-heavy areas. No plant is completely deer proof, but some choices are much less attractive to deer than others.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Are barberry bushes deer-resistant?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Yes, barberry is known for strong deer resistance, but Japanese barberry is invasive and should generally be avoided in Pennsylvania. Better deer-resistant alternatives may be a smarter choice.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 What are good deer-resistant flowers for the Poconos?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Daffodils, also called narcissus, are a strong spring choice because deer usually avoid them. Other options may include bleeding heart, anise hyssop, ornamental grasses, and certain native perennials depending on sun, shade, and soil conditions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Do you handle seasonal cleanups on this page?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Seasonal cleanups are offered separately. This landscaping page focuses on lawn mowing, weed control, mulch, planting, and basic landscape maintenance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa180\partightenfactor0

